      "problem": "If $a,b,$ and $c$ are elements of $S$, but $d$ and $e$ are not, then which of the following is true?",
      "worked_solution": "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $a,b,$ and $c$ are elements of $S,$ we write $a,b,c\\in S.$\n\n- Since $d$ and $e$ are *not* elements of $S,$ we write $d,e\\notin S.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $a,b,c\\in S$ and $d,e\\notin S$",
